               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>[second half of 13th cent.]</origDate>
                     <origPlace>[Italy]</origPlace>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance>
                     <p>On f. 1r, ownership inscriptions in sixteenth- to seventeenth-century hands
                        by <persName>Mosheh ben Natan (?) <foreign xml:lang="he">משה בן
                              נתן</foreign></persName>, <persName>Shmuʾel ben Mosheh of Ascolo
                              (<placeName key="place_113">Ascoli Piceno?</placeName>) <foreign
                              xml:lang="he">שמואל בן משה מאסקולו</foreign></persName> who was
                        probably the former's son, and <persName>Ezra of <placeName key="place_114"
                              >Fano</placeName>
                           <foreign xml:lang="he">עזרא מפאנו</foreign></persName>.</p>
                     <p>At the end of the manuscript, censorship certificates by <persName
                           key="person_315200936">Giovanni Domenico Carretto</persName> (<date
                           calendar="Gregorian">1617</date>, <locus>f. 92r</locus>); <persName
                           key="person_79251093">Dominico Irosolimitano</persName>, <persName
                           key="person_13163810144338820957">Alessandro Scipione</persName>, and
                           <persName key="person_16162179007907852870">Lorennzo Franguelo</persName>
                        (no date, <locus>f. 92v</locus>).</p></provenance>
                  <acquisition>It belonged to the library of <persName key="person_7753200">David
                        Oppenheim</persName> (<date calendar="Gregorian">1664-1736</date>), which
                     was purchased by the Bodleian Library in <date calendar="Gregorian"
                     >1829</date>.</acquisition>
               </history>
